    "## 2. Two-start relaxation time\n",
    "\n",
    "To extract a quantitative relaxation time, we use the **mutual cross-band criterion**. We evolve two identical systems in parallel: one starting from a random (infinite temperature) state and one from a fully ordered (zero temperature) state. \n",
    "\n",
    "Convergence is declared when both smoothed trajectories enter and sustain a band defined by the tail statistics of the other. This ensures that the system has \"forgotten\" its initial bias and is sampling from the true stationary distribution."
   ]
  },
